Translation patch: `StatusVarsIterator::next` and `StatusVars::get_status_var`

Change: In `next`, the length of the value (the `get_fixed!`/`get_var!` macro arithmetic) is computed by new helpers `value_len`/`var_len`/`db_names_len`/`skip_db_name` (the `for`/`while` loops of `UpdatedDbNames` become recursion) before `self.pos += len`; the `?`s become `match`es. `get_status_var`'s `self.iter().find_map(..)` becomes the recursive helper `find_status_var`.
Why: Aeneas does not support early returns (`?`) inside loops, `?` on `Option`, closures, or `find_map`.
Behaviour: Identical: the helpers read the same bytes in the same order as the macros, `self.pos` is advanced at the same points (by 1 for the key, then by `len` before the final `get`, which may still fail), and `None` is returned in the same cases; `find_status_var` calls `next` until a key matches or the iterator ends, which is `find_map`.

